(5068996, 737908, 52549, '<td valign="top">I love this. Great DOF, those gritty fingers, the b/w.... Wonderful shot! Congrats on the ribbon, Shannon.</td>', 'I love this. Great DOF, those gritty fingers, the b/w.... Wonderful shot! Congrats on the ribbon, Shannon.', '2008-11-18 00:46:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5069001, 737932, 68947, '<td valign="top">Steve,I found it pretty interesting actually!  I guess from the artist side of me, I see an artistic shot rather than the technicalities and this one hit me on the artistic side which really made me stop and look at it a lot more than some of the technically brilliant pieces.  To be perfectly honest (no disrespect intended to the ribboners at all)....I actually thought this was FAR more meaningful than the technically well done winning shots!  <br/> <br/>I''m afraid that being in here can be dangerous to artistic flare.  It trains AGAINST it in a lot of ways.  Our eyes are being trained to look at a photo for technical aspects and esthetics rather than anything really artistic.  You have an artistic eye.  Keep it that way.  DPC''ers will eventually evolve! ;)</td>', 'Steve,I found it pretty interesting actually!  I guess from the artist side of me, I see an artistic shot rather than the technicalities and this one hit me on the artistic side which really made me stop and look at it a lot more than some of the technically brilliant pieces.  To be perfectly honest (no disrespect intended to the ribboners at all)....I actually thought this was FAR more meaningful than the technically well done winning shots!   I''m afraid that being in here can be dangerous to artistic flare.  It trains AGAINST it in a lot of ways.  Our eyes are being trained to look at a photo for technical aspects and esthetics rather than anything really artistic.  You have an artistic eye.  Keep it that way.  DPC''ers will eventually evolve! ;)', '2008-11-18 00:47:22.000000', NULL, 0),
