(5069504, 737876, 29011, '<td valign="top">One of my faves as well. Congrats on the top5. I recognized the young lad , from the shot where he was painting the airplane model :) Didn''t rememer from which challenge it was from though.</td>', 'One of my faves as well. Congrats on the top5. I recognized the young lad , from the shot where he was painting the airplane model :) Didn''t rememer from which challenge it was from though.', '2008-11-18 12:42:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5069529, 737765, 30982, '<td valign="top">Pleased this was yours!  I do think if I am to continue playing with this stuff, I prefer the zone plate (or at least the way you shoot with a zone plate) to the pinhole.  You seem to get just a bit more depth and "focus" (relative, I know) and more pleasing color from it.  Or it could be you''re just really good.  At any rate, this ended up with a rather decent score, methinks.</td>', 'Pleased this was yours!  I do think if I am to continue playing with this stuff, I prefer the zone plate (or at least the way you shoot with a zone plate) to the pinhole.  You seem to get just a bit more depth and "focus" (relative, I know) and more pleasing color from it.  Or it could be you''re just really good.  At any rate, this ended up with a rather decent score, methinks.', '2008-11-18 12:57:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5069540, 737874, 52115, '<td valign="top">Poor Irene, you''re always "in the kitchen". At least you''re doing fun things in your kitchen, too. They use similar stuff (Tin-and-Lead alloy)for stained glass windows, too. This seems like a "Macro puzzle" photo.</td>', 'Poor Irene, you''re always "in the kitchen". At least you''re doing fun things in your kitchen, too. They use similar stuff (Tin-and-Lead alloy)for stained glass windows, too. This seems like a "Macro puzzle" photo.', '2008-11-18 13:04:45.000000', NULL, 0),
