(5077440, 737908, 15711, '<td valign="top">I think what I like most about this is the almost metallic feel to the entire tonal range.  Intense texture and detail.  Wonderful.  The message is loud and clear as well.  This would work well in a nat''l campaign by a non-profit organization for peace.  I can see it as a full page ad in a magazine. Well done and congrats.</td>', 'I think what I like most about this is the almost metallic feel to the entire tonal range.  Intense texture and detail.  Wonderful.  The message is loud and clear as well.  This would work well in a nat''l campaign by a non-profit organization for peace.  I can see it as a full page ad in a magazine. Well done and congrats.', '2008-11-21 10:02:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5077834, 737666, 54478, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club Eric!</b> <br/> <br/>First Impression: This photo fits into the challenge perfectly.<br/> <br/>Composition: Great composition. I like the large grouping of iron on the right, but I really like how smaller fillings fill the frame. The smaller fillings really add depth to the photo. The lighting also really adds depth to the photo by giving the filings some great shadows. The colors of the rust are also perfectly used. Good focus.<br/> <br/>Subject: I feel that the use if iron in this photo fits the challenge perfectly. I also really enjoy how you used the physical(magnetic) and chemical(rust/oxidation) properties of iron in your photo.<br/> <br/>Creativity: I find this photo very creative because of the reasons in my subject portion.<br/> <br/>Improvements: I am not sure if it is the texture of the iron filings or the use of USM, but edges of the filings almost seem too sharp and a little harsh. The filings are distracting to me. Softening up these edges a little bit would be a good improvement in my opinion.<br/> <br/>My Thoughts: The composition and the subject are just awesome. I study Physics and the fact you used the magnetic properties of iron shows your creativity. I could easily see a photo like this being used in physics texts or lectures. I honestly feel that not many of the photographers who scored higher than you showed there subject in a manor that truly reflects their particular element on the periodic table. You on the other hand, nailed it!<br/> <br/>Overall, great photo. I would score this a 9. If you have and questions please PM me. I hope my critique has been help and informative in some way.<br/> <br/>Cheers,<br/>Ron<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Eric!  First Impression: This photo fits into the challenge perfectly. Composition: Great composition. I like the large grouping of iron on the right, but I really like how smaller fillings fill the frame. The smaller fillings really add depth to the photo. The lighting also really adds depth to the photo by giving the filings some great shadows. The colors of the rust are also perfectly used. Good focus. Subject: I feel that the use if iron in this photo fits the challenge perfectly. I also really enjoy how you used the physical(magnetic) and chemical(rust/oxidation) properties of iron in your photo. Creativity: I find this photo very creative because of the reasons in my subject portion. Improvements: I am not sure if it is the texture of the iron filings or the use of USM, but edges of the filings almost seem too sharp and a little harsh. The filings are distracting to me. Softening up these edges a little bit would be a good improvement in my opinion. My Thoughts: The composition and the subject are just awesome. I study Physics and the fact you used the magnetic properties of iron shows your creativity. I could easily see a photo like this being used in physics texts or lectures. I honestly feel that not many of the photographers who scored higher than you showed there subject in a manor that truly reflects their particular element on the periodic table. You on the other hand, nailed it! Overall, great photo. I would score this a 9. If you have and questions please PM me. I hope my critique has been help and informative in some way. Cheers,Ron ', '2008-11-21 14:40:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5077908, 737867, 86090, '<td valign="top">Is this the same place where <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=27133" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">judi</a> took the picture for the blue challenge? I really love, love her work, but on this one, the colors on yours makes it looks more beautiful, amazing!!!</td>', 'Is this the same place where  judi took the picture for the blue challenge? I really love, love her work, but on this one, the colors on yours makes it looks more beautiful, amazing!!!', '2008-11-21 16:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5078173, 737857, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>I am not sure what to say about this picture. I checked your website and you do have good stuff, natural and good stuff but I must say this doesn''t look like one of your work.<br/> <br/>but anyway, let''s get down the business.<br/> <br/>I have no idea Surprisium, I think it means something about surprise?<br/> <br/>I like 1 quarter of this photo which is standing out pretty good. I don''t like the way sky, clouds and wires on the window but only the face. I am not even sure if that''s your place, or someone else''s, if you did have chance, I would suggest you to wait a bit more, have sun go down a bit more, darker outside and lighter inside... even a little spotlight on the face could be pretty interesting.<br/> <br/>This photo looks like entered just to see what people would say rather than competing in the challenge.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work (not this, this is horrible) and show us better work of yours :)<br/> <br/>and thanks for the great work you have done for DCP community :) we all appreciated.<br/> <br/>Leo<br/> <br/>Edited to fix a Word character in here :P<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-22 03:17:14.</i></td>', 'Hello from Critique Club :) I am not sure what to say about this picture. I checked your website and you do have good stuff, natural and good stuff but I must say this doesn''t look like one of your work. but anyway, let''s get down the business. I have no idea Surprisium, I think it means something about surprise? I like 1 quarter of this photo which is standing out pretty good. I don''t like the way sky, clouds and wires on the window but only the face. I am not even sure if that''s your place, or someone else''s, if you did have chance, I would suggest you to wait a bit more, have sun go down a bit more, darker outside and lighter inside... even a little spotlight on the face could be pretty interesting. This photo looks like entered just to see what people would say rather than competing in the challenge. Keep up the good work (not this, this is horrible) and show us better work of yours :) and thanks for the great work you have done for DCP community :) we all appreciated. Leo Edited to fix a Word character in here :P', '2008-11-21 20:29:14.000000', '2008-11-22 03:17:14.000000', 0),
(5078190, 737946, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Oh man, you do have great imagination. I don''t care about the challenge subject, but I will get down to this picture without thinking if matches to the challenge or not.<br/> <br/>Technically, perfect. I like the sharpness. Very well exposed. I love the composition, with ring, the black area on the right and angle... I also like the framing.<br/> <br/>I think this is one of the good works I saw in DPC with one color. This should have been around 6.2<br/> <br/>I checked out your photos, and you do have talent. You have big imagination and ability to capture them. Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from Critique Club :) Oh man, you do have great imagination. I don''t care about the challenge subject, but I will get down to this picture without thinking if matches to the challenge or not. Technically, perfect. I like the sharpness. Very well exposed. I love the composition, with ring, the black area on the right and angle... I also like the framing. I think this is one of the good works I saw in DPC with one color. This should have been around 6.2 I checked out your photos, and you do have talent. You have big imagination and ability to capture them. Keep up the good work. Leo', '2008-11-21 20:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5078202, 737774, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Nice sharp image with little over exposed white areas at the end of the balloon. It probably exposed little wrong and probably some work done to fix it. I might be way off, but this photo looks like 1-good imagination 2-bad execution of the imagination.<br/> <br/>Too much dark area on your photo, you should not have the tied end of the balloon right on the middle of the frame. Talking about the frame, if you did have a thin red frame with this photo, it would look much better. Try to see it bit more cropped, and next time try to give a bit softer light, I think there is a flash or something used that''s shining too much on tip of the balloon.<br/> <br/>Keep on clicking, you will get there, I have no doubt :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from Critique Club :) Nice sharp image with little over exposed white areas at the end of the balloon. It probably exposed little wrong and probably some work done to fix it. I might be way off, but this photo looks like 1-good imagination 2-bad execution of the imagination. Too much dark area on your photo, you should not have the tied end of the balloon right on the middle of the frame. Talking about the frame, if you did have a thin red frame with this photo, it would look much better. Try to see it bit more cropped, and next time try to give a bit softer light, I think there is a flash or something used that''s shining too much on tip of the balloon. Keep on clicking, you will get there, I have no doubt :) Leo', '2008-11-21 20:43:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5078232, 737841, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>I see steel more than aluminum, but I don''t care what the subject is, let''s take a look at the photo.<br/> <br/>Nice colors, sharp and nice focus on the edge of the "thing" You should have dodge the bright area a little bit more, but it''s not that bad. I like the lighting here, from back, the shadows are the main attraction (I know you were hoping people would like them too).<br/> <br/>Having three dimension look on your photo is giving much better feeling rather than a flat photo.<br/> <br/>I believe 5.8 for this photo is pretty much on target... over average. The composition got you a good points, sharpness and color also got you some more good votes.<br/> <br/>If you had only the front end of this thing and not the back of it, I think it would look better. Don''t cut it, whatever this is, but put cardboard or paper behind it, and shoot it that way. You won''t have many shadows in the back, but I like cleaner photos :)<br/> <br/>I checked your page, photos look very nice. You do have a style, develop that and you might be one of kind.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work, and practice without mercy :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from Critique Club :) I see steel more than aluminum, but I don''t care what the subject is, let''s take a look at the photo. Nice colors, sharp and nice focus on the edge of the "thing" You should have dodge the bright area a little bit more, but it''s not that bad. I like the lighting here, from back, the shadows are the main attraction (I know you were hoping people would like them too). Having three dimension look on your photo is giving much better feeling rather than a flat photo. I believe 5.8 for this photo is pretty much on target... over average. The composition got you a good points, sharpness and color also got you some more good votes. If you had only the front end of this thing and not the back of it, I think it would look better. Don''t cut it, whatever this is, but put cardboard or paper behind it, and shoot it that way. You won''t have many shadows in the back, but I like cleaner photos :) I checked your page, photos look very nice. You do have a style, develop that and you might be one of kind. Keep up the good work, and practice without mercy :) Leo', '2008-11-21 20:57:25.000000', NULL, 0),
